{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/4076","id":4922045919,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-508s8AAAABJWB13w","html_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/4076","diff_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/4076.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/4076.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/4076","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/4076/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/4076/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/4076/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/statuses/9744f9df268590295a9872b1952c695a678192b9","number":4076,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Conditional κ = 0.001730809033576552081734 (+1.458e-7 over #3945): three staged helper entries and an LP-exact T360 fill","user":{"login":"rohanarun","id":11659839,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjU5ODM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11659839?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun","html_url":"https://github.com/rohanarun","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanarun/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Author-checked conditional candidate; not maintainer-reviewed.** This stages three more helpers on #3945's staged544 words and builds a new literal T360 owner fill.\n\n**Result.** The new complete moment root lies in **[0.001730809033576552081734, 0.001730809033576552081735]**, so\n\nκ = 0.001730809033576552081734 − 10⁻⁴⁶ − 10⁻⁷⁰\n\nThat is **+1.458·10⁻⁷ over #3945 (+0.0084%)**. It inherits #3945's source, hosting, analytic and multiplication-model hypotheses.\n\n| | #3945 | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| local profile per call | `{1:2482, 2:712, 3:218, 4:109, 5:20, 8:8}` | `{1:2488, 2:714, 3:223, 4:102, 5:20, 8:8}` |\n| helper widths 5/6/7/8/9 | 28 / 18 / 53 / 96 / 213 | 28 / 18 / **56 / 93** / 213 |\n| owner idle | `{3:23328, 5:4320, 48:137952}` | `{3:22842, 5:1890, 48:138438}` |\n| root lower bound | 0.001730663236534549309146 | **0.001730809033576552081734** |\n\n**Construction.**\n- **Words.** Helpers 608, 609 and 600 each get one extra entrance dimension, lose four early ¼-weight reads, and gain two exact releases after a common cut. This follows #3949's staged-entry construction, extended so releases can land in other helpers. Each of the three narrows from width 8 to width 7.\n- **Frames and cleanup.** The exact frame optimum is written back into A/B/restore, and cleanup is re-derived literally. Source-guarded literal records under `recipe/` replay without any solver.\n- **Owner fill.** A new literal T360 owner fill moves 70,876 of #3945's 1,321,920 roles (`owner/MOVES.json.gz`) and reaches the window-free pattern-LP optimum for the narrowed inventory.\n\n**Replay** (Python 3.12, standard library only):\n```sh\npython3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/staged544-triple-entry-fill\n```\nThat gives `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE`, with all registered commands passing:\n- word reconstruction and arbitrary-dirty semantics;\n- an independent GF(2) frame ledger, with 10 controls;\n- the exact rational root, with 4 controls;\n- a full owner audit of every role in both fills, with 7 controls;\n- byte-equal fill regeneration;\n- recipe controls in both normal and optimized Python.\n\nFresh five-stage native runs pass for both changed words. The root bracket was also re-checked with a second, independent rational engine.\n\n**Admission status (stated plainly).** `admission/full_replay.py` rebuilds #3945's closure plus the six staged-entry files and runs the inherited admission engine end to end. Every stage through the outer ledger and the independent outer check passed. **The final release stage is still pending.** It was still running when this was submitted, and it needs at least 8 GB of RAM with `--jobs 1`. `admission/authenticate.py` is therefore not in VERIFY.json yet.\n\n**Credit.**\n- Staged-entry mechanism: Ross Richardson (#3605) and dataisfire (#3734).\n- Census and assembler: ChaloupeMusic / Erwan Secousses (#3949).\n- T360 clock and fill: #3815, with #3638 lineage.\n- Terminal-width-5 words, owner walk, frame walker, root enclosures, native runner and admission adaptation: Dugongue (#3945).\n- Exact frame solver: Marius-Paul Dumitrean.\n- Audit core: Sagar Thakrar (#3687) and roger-sato (#3693).\n- Comparison claim: zxv (#3682).\n- Independent audits of #3945 (#3969, #3987, #3994) were read.\n\nNOTICE.md has the full lineage.\n\n**Open next questions.**\n- A fourth 8→7 entry loses about 9.06·10⁻⁸. Could a staged entry that narrows a width-9 or width-7 helper pay instead?\n- Are there more release triads like 608/609/610? Swapping 600 for a 608-type helper would give roughly +1.74·10⁻⁷.\n- Is there a smaller move set or a clock change that admits a cheaper narrowing schedule?\n\nPrepared by Rohan Arun with Anthropic Claude assistance.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01F5n4jqR72j3QDY71gGBVb1\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_loc